From 196291efafa727cf5a4f1948e2350dca769e3173 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omalawn <omalawn@local>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:07:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] omalawn locked update: update status, and a locked phone
 installs at its next unlock

New command launcher.update_status reports the last update's outcome
(installed, pending_user_action, deferred, failed with a reason), kept in
the omalawn_update_status preferences. A silent update offered while the
phone is locked is not committed at once (seen on a locked Samsung S23:
the session may never finish); its session is kept and committed the next
time the phone is unlocked, from the link service's ACTION_USER_PRESENT /
ACTION_SCREEN_ON receiver, and the answer says deferred_until_unlock: true.
A deferred update lost to a restart is installed again from the kept file
with a new session, or recorded as failed when the file is gone.
